Given a binary tree where each node holds a digit (0–9):
	•	Each root-to-leaf path forms a number by concatenating the digits along the path.
	•	Example paths you mentioned:
	•	1 → 2 → 4 → number 124
	•	1 → 2 → 5 → number 125
	•	(If there’s another path like 1 → 3 → 5, that would be 135, etc.)
	•	The task is to sum all such numbers formed from every root-to-leaf path.

So for paths:
	•	1 → 2 → 4 → 124
	•	1 → 2 → 5 → 125
	•	1 → 2 → 5 (if duplicate / another subtree) → 125

The total sum would be: 124 + 125 + 125.


